Selection rule (reproducible without a script; this is what was run)
  1. Walk css/css-grid/ excluding directories named crashtests (vendored in
     tests/wpt/css-grid-crashtests/) and grid-lanes (ADR 031).
  2. A file is a candidate if it has a <link> whose rel contains "match" or
     "mismatch". Read with an HTML tokenizer, not a regex.
  3. Drop the candidate if it is not .html/.htm, if it has rel=mismatch, or if
     it contains a <script> element or any attribute whose name starts with
     "on" (the same test reftest.rs's needs_script applies). Scripted tests are
     counted as dropped-scripted.
  4. Resolve the single rel=match href against the test's own directory
     (absolute /css/css-grid/... hrefs resolve inside the module).
  5. Drop the pair if the reference is not .html/.htm, is outside css/css-grid/
     (or inside grid-lanes), is missing, or itself contains script or on*
     attributes (none did).
  6. Vendor the test, its reference (once if shared), and any file named by
     <link rel=stylesheet href>, <img src>, <source|video|audio|iframe|embed
     src> or <object data> in either, if that file exists inside css/css-grid/.

Known gaps that remain in the denominator (nothing was removed to hide them)
  128 kept pairs link a stylesheet that is not in the pinned sparse checkout and
